   $q$A ball dropped from a 64 foot bridge has height $h(t) = -16t^2 + 64$ feet after $t$ seconds, for $0 \le t \le 2$. Which formula gives the time $t$ at which the ball is at height $h$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$t = \\frac{\\sqrt{64 - h}}{4}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$t = \\frac{\\sqrt{h - 64}}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-isolating-square"},{"text":"$t = -\\frac{\\sqrt{64 - h}}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"chose-negative-root"},{"text":"$t = \\frac{\\sqrt{64 - h}}{16}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-root-of-coefficient"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$t = \frac{\sqrt{64 - h}}{4}$$q$, $q$$16t^2 = 64 - h$, so $t^2 = \frac{64 - h}{16}$ and, since $t \ge 0$, $t = \frac{\sqrt{64 - h}}{4}$; at $h = 28$ this gives $t = \frac{6}{4} = 1.5$, and $h(1.5) = 28$. The negative root gives negative times, outside the restricted domain.$q$, 'draft', null)
